Why: Same change as 
patches/mono-1.2.6/0006-profiler-aot-include-config.patch, rebased onto 
mono-1.9.1.1. mono-profiler-aot.c tests PLATFORM_WIN32 to choose the 
one-argument  Windows mkdir(), but never includes <config.h>, so the POSIX 
mkdir(path,  0777) branch is compiled and mingw-w64 GCC errors 'too many 
arguments to  function mkdir'.  Include config.h.  New patch (not in Guix). 
 

diff --git a/mono/profiler/mono-profiler-aot.c b/mono/profiler/mono-profiler-aot.c
index 72c603ca..5babb7a5 100644
--- a/mono/profiler/mono-profiler-aot.c
+++ b/mono/profiler/mono-profiler-aot.c
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#include <config.h>
 #include <mono/metadata/profiler.h>
 #include <mono/metadata/tokentype.h>
 #include <mono/metadata/tabledefs.h>
